var(--covered)"></span><b>16</b><span class=3D"lbl">fully covered</span></d=
iv>
      <div class=3D"legend-row"><span class=3D"swatch" style=3D"background:=
var(--partial)"></span><b>3</b><span class=3D"lbl">touched, not designed</s=
pan></div>
      <div class=3D"legend-row"><span class=3D"swatch" style=3D"background:=
var(--gap)"></span><b>1</b><span class=3D"lbl">absent</span></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class=3D"phase">
    <div class=3D"phase-head">
      <span class=3D"phase-tag">01</span>
      <h2>Problem Framing &amp; Discovery</h2>
    </div>
    <div class=3D"ledger">
      <details class=3D"item">
        <summary><span class=3D"idx">1.1</span><span class=3D"item-name">Fe=
ature =E2=86=92 business-outcome reframing</span><span class=3D"badge cover=
ed">Covered</span></summary>
        <div class=3D"body">The doc explicitly separates "ask questions in =
one place" from the real deliverable =E2=80=94 grounded, cited, permission-=
safe answers. <span class=3D"ref">=C2=A71</span></div>
      </details>
      <details class=3D"item">
        <summary><span class=3D"idx">1.2</span><span class=3D"item-name">St=
akeholder / persona mapping</span><span class=3D"badge covered">Covered</sp=
an></summary>
        <div class=3D"body">Four-role table (end user, operator, security o=
wner, exec sponsor) each with a distinct success condition and failure sign=
ature. <span class=3D"ref">=C2=A71</span></div>
      </details>
      <details class=3D"item">
        <summary><span class=3D"idx">1.3</span><span class=3D"item-name">Cl=
arifying questions that move architecture</span><span class=3D"badge covere=
d">Covered</span></summary>
        <div class=3D"body">Question list is explicitly filtered to ones th=
at change scope, risk, or component choice =E2=80=94 not generic intake. <s=
pan class=3D"ref">=C2=A72</span></div>
      </details>
      <details class=3D"item">
        <summary><span class=3D"idx">1.4</span><span class=3D"item-name">Re=
quirements split + prioritization (MoSCoW)</span><span class=3D"badge cover=
ed">Covered</span></summary>
        <div class=3D"body">Functional vs. non-functional requirements, the=
n must/should/could tiers tied to launch gates. <span class=3D"ref">=C2=A72=
</span></div>
      </details>
      <details class=3D"item">
        <summary><span class=3D"idx">1.5</span><span class=3D"item-name">Ex=
plicit non-goals / scope fence</span><span class=3D"badge covered">Covered<=
/span></summary>
        <div class=3D"body">A named exclusion list (no downstream actions, =
no editing, no cross-tenant search) prevents platform sprawl. <span class=
=3D"ref">=C2=A72</span></div>
      </details>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class=3D"phase">
    <div class=3D"phase-head">
      <span class=3D"phase-tag">02</span>
      <h2>Estimation &amp; Architecture</h2>
    </div>
    <div class=3D"ledger">
      <details class=3D"item">
        <summary><span class=3D"idx">2.1</span><span class=3D"item-name">Ba=
ck-of-envelope scale &amp; capacity math</span><span class=3D"badge covered=
">Covered</span></summary>
        <div class=3D"body">Explicit round assumptions (employees, chunks, =
avg/peak QPS) used to justify architecture, plus a sensitivity table. <span=
 class=3D"ref">=C2=A73</span></div>
      </details>
      <details class=3D"item">
        <summary><span class=3D"idx">2.2</span><span class=3D"item-name">Un=
it economics / cost-driver breakdown</span><span class=3D"badge covered">Co=
vered</span></summary>
        <div class=3D"body">Embedding, index, and model-token cost estimate=
d independently with separate owners; cost-per-answered-query tracked post-=
launch. <span class=3D"ref">=C2=A73, =C2=A77</span></div>
      </details>
      <details class=3D"item">
        <summary><span class=3D"idx">2.3</span><span class=3D"item-name">En=
d-to-end architecture &amp; data flow</span><span class=3D"badge covered">C=
overed</span></summary>
        <div class=3D"body">Control/data plane split, full component invent=
ory, and an 11-step happy-path sequence narrated in order. <span class=3D"r=
ef">=C2=A74</span></div>
      </details>
      <details class=3D"item">
        <summary><span class=3D"idx">2.4</span><span class=3D"item-name">Da=
ta model &amp; API contracts</span><span class=3D"badge covered">Covered</s=
pan></summary>
        <div class=3D"body">Three typed records, four REST contracts with e=
xplicit error semantics and idempotency rules. <span class=3D"ref">=C2=A75<=
/span></div>
      </details>
      <details class=3D"item">
        <summary><span class=3D"idx">2.5</span><span class=3D"item-name">Bu=
ild-vs-buy / vendor &amp; model-selection trade-off</span><span class=3D"ba=
dge gap">Absent</span></summary>
        <div class=3D"body">No comparison of managed vs. self-hosted vector=
 stores, or proprietary vs. open-weight model choice on cost/latency/qualit=
y. The chapter deliberately stays vendor-agnostic =E2=80=94 worth adding as=
 your own layer if a panel probes it.</div>
      </details>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class=3D"phase">
    <div class=3D"phase-head">
      <span class=3D"phase-tag">03</span>
      <h2>Trade-offs, Security &amp; Reliability</h2>
    </div>
    <div class=3D"ledger">
      <details class=3D"item">
        <summary><span class=3D"idx">3.1</span><span class=3D"item-name">Na=
med trade-off pairs with a balanced verdict</span><span class=3D"badge cove=
red">Covered</span></summary>
        <div class=3D"body">Four trade-offs argued both ways then resolved:=
 hybrid vs. vector-only, query-time vs. precomputed ACLs, context size vs. =
cost, real-time vs. scheduled sync. <span class=3D"ref">=C2=A78</span></div=
>
      </details>
      <details class=3D"item">
        <summary><span class=3D"idx">3.2</span><span class=3D"item-name">Se=
curity threat model + fail-open/closed policy</span><span class=3D"badge co=
vered">Covered</span></summary>
        <div class=3D"body">Four boundary questions (retrieve / show / log =
/ degrade), plus a per-component fail-open-or-closed table. <span class=3D"=
ref">=C2=A76</span></div>
      </details>
      <details class=3D"item">
        <summary><span class=3D"idx">3.3</span><span class=3D"item-name">Fa=
ilure-mode drills, not just a components list</span><span class=3D"badge co=
vered">Covered</span></summary>
        <div class=3D"body">A single failure (missed deletion event) walked=
 through detect =E2=86=92 contain =E2=86=92 recover, then generalized into =
a detect/contain/recover/prevent table. <span class=3D"ref">=C2=A76</span><=
/div>
      </details>
      <details class=3D"item">
        <summary><span class=3D"idx">3.4</span><span class=3D"item-name">Te=
sting strategy (contract + failure-injection)</span><span class=3D"badge co=
vered">Covered</span></summary>
        <div class=3D"body">Runnable pytest sketches proving the permission=
 gate fires before generation, and that malformed metadata fails closed. <s=
pan class=3D"ref">=C2=A75, =C2=A76</span></div>
      </details>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class=3D"phase">
    <div class=3D"phase-head">
      <span class=3D"phase-tag">04</span>
      <h2>Delivery, Governance &amp; Communication</h2>
    </div>
    <div class=3D"ledger">
      <details class=3D"item">
        <summary><span class=3D"idx">4.1</span><span class=3D"item-name">La=
yered evaluation metrics &amp; observability</span><span class=3D"badge cov=
ered">Covered</span></summary>
        <div class=3D"body">Four-layer dashboard (technical health / model =
quality / adoption / business outcome) so no single metric gets over-optimi=
zed. <span class=3D"ref">=C2=A77</span></div>
      </details>
      <details class=3D"item">
        <summary><span class=3D"idx">4.2</span><span class=3D"item-name">Ph=
ased rollout, risk register, rollback gates</span><span class=3D"badge cove=
red">Covered</span></summary>
        <div class=3D"body">Four-stage rollout with a named exit criterion =
at each stage, plus an owner/mitigation/trigger risk register. <span class=
=3D"ref">=C2=A77</span></div>
      </details>
      <details class=3D"item">
        <summary><span class=3D"idx">4.3</span><span class=3D"item-name">Re=
gulatory &amp; data-governance depth</span><span class=3D"badge partial">Pa=
rtial</span></summary>
        <div class=3D"body">Residency and retention appear only as a discov=
ery question and a retention-window config knob =E2=80=94 there's no design=
ed answer for data residency across regions, right-to-erasure across derive=
d embeddings, or audit-retention conflicts with privacy law.</div>
      </details>
      <details class=3D"item">
        <summary><span class=3D"idx">4.4</span><span class=3D"item-name">Re=
sponsible-AI framing beyond hallucination</span><span class=3D"badge partia=
l">Partial</span></summary>
        <div class=3D"body">Grounding, citations, and abstention cover fact=
uality =E2=80=94 but nothing addresses retrieval bias across departments/la=
nguages, or equitable answer quality across employee groups.</div>
      </details>
      <details class=3D"item">
        <summary><span class=3D"idx">4.5</span><span class=3D"item-name">Ch=
ange-management / org adoption narrative</span><span class=3D"badge partial=
">Partial</span></summary>
        <div class=3D"body">Training and documentation are named as operati=
onal owners, but there's no executive-facing adoption narrative =E2=80=94 h=
ow you sell the rollout internally, manage champions, or handle resistance =
from teams the assistant displaces.</div>
      </details>
      <details class=3D"item">
        <summary><span class=3D"idx">4.6</span><span class=3D"item-name">Ti=
